"""Integration test infrastructure.

This package provides hermetic services for integration tests using rules_itest.

rules_itest usage:
- Best for first-party Go/Node/Python binaries as test services
- Supports automatic port assignment, health checks, hot-reload with ibazel
- See https://github.com/dzbarsky/rules_itest for docs

For PostgreSQL tests:
- Use testcontainers (see props/testing/fixtures/db.py)
- BCR postgres module only provides libpq (client), not server binaries
- rules_postgresql builds from source on Linux (slow) and isn't in BCR

Example rules_itest service (when we have first-party services to test):

    load("@rules_itest//:itest.bzl", "itest_service")

    itest_service(
        name = "my_service",
        exe = "//path/to:binary",
        autoassign_port = True,
        http_health_check_address = "http://localhost:$${PORT}/health",
    )
"""
